==English==
[[File:Emys orbicularis 2009 G1.jpg|thumb|European pond terrapin, Emys orbicularis]]
[[File:Red-eared sliders and Mallard in Golden Gate Park 1.jpg|thumb|Red-eared terrapins, Trachemys scripta elegans]]

===Etymology===
From an {{der|en|alg}} word ''torope'' ("little [[turtle]]"); compare {{cog|abe|tolba||turtle}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtɛɹəpɪn/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-terrapin.wav |Audio (UK)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any of several [[small]] [[turtle]]s, of the [[family|families]] [[Emydidae]] and [[Geoemydidae]], that live in [[fresh]] or [[brackish]] [[water]].

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|red-eared terrapin}}
* {{l|en|salt-marsh terrapin}}

